{
  "vector_set": "gateway-mqtt-canonical-json/v1",
  "scope": "Runtime-gateway MQTT envelope authentication (HMAC preimage and AES-GCM AAD). This is NOT evidence/v2. Evidence artifacts control their numeric domain and impose the D-011 agreement zone; gateway MQTT transports operational sensor and reasoning data whose numeric range is broader, so D-011 MUST NOT be enforced here.",
  "purpose": "Cross-language agreement between the Python runtime and the Go gateway. An implementation passes when serialising `value` yields exactly `canonical_utf8_hex`, and when every entry under `refused` is rejected.",
  "rules": {
    "key_order": "lexicographic by Unicode scalar value (code point) at every nesting level, applied recursively. NOT UTF-16 code unit order: the two disagree across the BMP/astral boundary, see key_order_astral_vs_bmp.",
    "separators": "',' and ':' with no whitespace outside string values",
    "escaping": "RFC 8259. Escape only '\"' and '\\\\' plus C0 controls; short escapes \\b \\f \\n \\r \\t; other C0 as \\u00xx lowercase. Every other scalar is emitted literally, including < > & U+2028 U+2029 DEL and all non-ASCII.",
    "numbers": "A verifier preserves the number spelling received on the wire. The producer already emitted its own canonical form, so reproducing that text reproduces the preimage. A verifier MUST NOT re-format numbers: that would diverge from the producer and would impose an evidence-storage constraint on operational telemetry. Producers MUST NOT emit NaN or Infinity, which are not valid JSON.",
    "unicode": "Payload bytes must be valid UTF-8 and must not contain unpaired surrogate escapes.",
    "refusal_basis": "'divergence': the two stock serialisers produce different bytes, so accepting the value would break signature agreement. 'invalid_json': rejected by any conforming parser."
  },
